  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The least distance of vision of a long sighted person is $60 \\mathrm{cm}$. By using a spectacle lens, this distance is reduced to $12 \\mathrm{cm}$. The power of the lens is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "nfrpe",
      "text": "$+5.0 D$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "vAtfr",
      "text": "$(20 / 3) \\mathrm{D}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "NHjYb",
      "text": "$-(10 / 3)$ D",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "YOqgj",
      "text": "$+2.0 \\mathrm{D}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Here, $v=-60 \\mathrm{cm}, u=-12 \\mathrm{cm}$\r\n$\\therefore$ By using the relation, $\\frac{1}{f}=\\frac{1}{v}-\\frac{1}{u}$\r\nWe have. $\\frac{1}{f}=\\frac{1}{-60}-\\frac{1}{-12}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\frac{1}{f}=\\frac{1}{15} \\mathrm{cm}$ or $\\frac{100}{15} \\mathrm{m}$\r\nSo, the power of lens, $P=\\frac{100}{15}=+\\frac{20}{3} \\mathrm{D}$",
    "image": null
  },
